%N A400122 Number of unlabeled reducible flow graphs with n nodes containing a global source and a global sink, self-loops allowed.
%C A400122 Self-loops on the source or sink are impossible; loops occur on the other n-2 nodes only.
%C A400122 Computed exactly by the equivariant Burnside recurrence (see _reducible_unlabeled in the linked program of A397968).
%D A400122 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A400122 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A400122 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A400122 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A400122 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%F A400122 The same Burnside sum and equivariant source-sink recurrence as the loopless version, with an additional factor 2^c(mu) for the invariant self-loops on the cycles of the n-2 non-endpoint vertices.
%o A400122 (Python) unlabeled_reducible_sequence("unlabeled_reducible_ss_single_sink_loops", 16) # See Python link in A397968 for program code.
%Y A400122 Cf. A397968 (entry-pointed loopless family), A350794, A351052.
%K A400122 nonn,new
%O A400122 1,3
